#AUTO 12
#NEEDED 0
# Generic-timer recon (issue 110n / phase-2 prep).
#
# The ARM architected timer is a counter every core carries that ticks at a
# fixed frequency, independent of the CPU clock — so it keeps real wall-clock
# time even as the CPU clock changes. This probe reads that frequency
# (CNTFRQ_EL0) and the counter (CNTPCT_EL0) twice across a fixed nop delay,
# so the delta is a real elapsed span. It answers three things at once:
#   - what frequency firmware programmed the timer at (expected ~24 MHz),
#   - how long our nop-counted busy_delay REALLY is (to calibrate delay_busy),
#   - and it de-risks phase-2 scheduling, which leans on this counter.
#
# Read-only: the counter and frequency registers are read via MRS, done in C
# (the interpreter's R only touches MMIO). Priority 12 puts it right after the
# health check — it is foundational (measurement) and unblocks later probes
# and dumps that want to report real time.

CALL timer_recon
